WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.287
A scatter plot is one of the most useful visuals when both variables are numeric.

00:00:05.287 --> 00:00:08.592
Each point represents one observation.

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:14.822
One variable is placed on the horizontal axis and the other on the vertical axis.

00:00:14.822 --> 00:00:22.515
The pattern of points can tell us about direction, shape, strength, clusters, and unusual observations.

00:00:22.973 --> 00:00:26.755
Run the example and look at amount versus satisfaction.

00:00:26.755 --> 00:00:32.230
Before calculating any correlation coefficient, describe what you see.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:36.385
Do higher amounts generally appear with higher satisfaction?

00:00:36.385 --> 00:00:38.630
Is the pattern roughly linear?

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.850
Are there unusual points?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:48.835
This visual inspection is important because a single number can hide nonlinear patterns or influential observations.

00:00:48.835 --> 00:00:54.527
A good workflow is plot first, summarize second, interpret last.
